    "Card 2: the teacher's remarks that the first shooter must go and slaughter it (0:02:54–0:03:08) and that hide/bones remain usable and belong to the first (0:03:45–0:04:00) are his, labelled «استاد». His reason for case 1 («صحیح سلامت جانور کی طرح تھا») differs in wording from the matn's «لأنه هو الآخذ… الصيد لمن أخذ»; both given, labelled. The madhbuh-level exception (0:05:07–0:06:06) matches the matn «لا يبقى فيه من الحياة إلا بقدر ما يبقى في المذبوح… يحل»; the goat example is his. The footnote «فصار الجواب إلخ» (v7 338) has no source → S(«حاشیہ ص ٣٣٨»). The نصب الراية footnote (v7 337–338, «*غريب… [نصب الراية ٤/ ٣١٨-٣١٩]») is tagged as printed (vol-first); its OCR «أذاره» read as «أثاره», «فدفعتهما الثلثة» = the third (Iraqi) girl.",
    "Card 3: teacher slip 0:10:31 «تین روپے یعنی… تین ہزار روپے» (means 3,000). At 0:10:09 he sums «تین ہزار… دو ہزار میں… پانچ ہزار» (interim), final total 8,000 (0:10:31) — matches البناية ٥٣٧/١١ (10 dirhams: 2 + 3 + 3 = 8). His reason at 0:07:15–0:07:24 for the daman (the prey would have been halal either way) is closer to the book's reason for the THIRD (meat) daman; the book's reason for the basic daman is destroying the first man's owned, already-reduced prey (v7 339). Card labels the teacher's words and gives the matn. The teacher does not name «الزيادات». The البناية ٥٣٧/١١ footnote is partly duplicated/garbled in OCR (v7 339 lines «وإن كان تفويت اللحم فيه موجود…»); only the clear part is used. OCR v7 340 matn «فهذا بالرمي الثاني… فيدخله» read with الكفاية ٦٣/٩ as «فهو… فيضمنه».",
